The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
vc4_bo_cache_destroy(dev);
if (vc4->hang_state)
    vc4_free_hang_state(dev, vc4->hang_state);
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the `vc4_bo_cache_destroy(dev)` function is called before the hang state is freed. If the hang state is still allocated when the BO cache is being destroyed, it can lead to an error since the cache will attempt to free buffer objects that are still in use, resulting in a conflict.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (vc4->hang_state)
    vc4_free_hang_state(dev, vc4->hang_state);
vc4_bo_cache_destroy(dev);
```
Reason:
The fix involves rearranging the order of operations so that the hang state is freed before the BO cache is destroyed. This ensures that there are no remaining references to the hang state when the cache attempts to free its allocated buffer objects, thus preventing the error that occurs during the destruction process.

